  <bp:ProteinReference xmlns:bp="http://www.biopax.org/release/biopax-level3.owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" rdf:ID="ProteinReference14">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q9UBR2 CTSZ</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CTSZ</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref115" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Exhibits carboxy-monopeptidase as well as carboxy-dipeptidase activity (PubMed:10504234). Capable of producing kinin potentiating peptides (By similarity).CATALYTIC ACTIVITY Release of C-terminal amino acid residues with broad specificity, but lacks action on C-terminal proline. Shows weak endopeptidase activity.ACTIVITY REGULATION The disulfide bridge formed between Cys-33 in the propeptide and the active site residue Cys-92 may prevent activation of the zymogen through formation of a reversible covalent bond with the active site residue.INTERACTION Widely expressed.SIMILARITY Belongs to the peptidase C1 family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
