  <bp:ProteinReference xmlns:bp="http://www.biopax.org/release/biopax-level3.owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" rdf:ID="ProteinReference18">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q9H0V9 LMAN2L</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LMAN2L</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">VIPL</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PSEC0028</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UNQ368/PRO704</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref150" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION May be involved in the regulation of export from the endoplasmic reticulum of a subset of glycoproteins. May function as a regulator of ERGIC-53.INTERACTION Predominantly found in the endoplasmic reticulum. Partly found in the Golgi.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS Expressed in numerous tissues. Highest expression in skeletal muscle and kidney, intermediate levels in heart, liver and placenta, low levels in brain, thymus, spleen, small intestine and lung.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
