  <bp:ProteinReference xmlns:bp="http://www.biopax.org/release/biopax-level3.owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" rdf:ID="ProteinReference41">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:O15498 YKT6</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">YKT6</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref309" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Vesicular soluble NSF attachment protein receptor (v-SNARE) mediating vesicle docking and fusion to a specific acceptor cellular compartment (PubMed:9211930, PubMed:15215310). Functions in endoplasmic reticulum to Golgi transport; as part of a SNARE complex composed of GOSR1, GOSR2 and STX5 (By similarity). Functions in early/recycling endosome to TGN transport; as part of a SNARE complex composed of BET1L, GOSR1 and STX5 (PubMed:15215310). Has a S-palmitoyl transferase activity (PubMed:15479160, PubMed:15044687). Essential for the structural and functional organization of the Golgi apparatus (PubMed:32128853).SUBUNIT Identified in 2 different SNARE complexes; the first one composed of GOSR1, GOSR2 and STX5 and the second one composed of BET1L, GOSR1 and STX5.INTERACTION Probably cycles through vesicles between Golgi and endosomes.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS The longin domain regulates palmitoylation and membrane targeting (PubMed:32128853).DOMAIN The CAAX motif is a signal for farnesylation at Cys-195 and the subsequent geranylgeranylation at Cys-194; the double prenylation is essential for the structural and functional organization of the Golgi apparatus (PubMed:32128853).PTM Palmitoylated; catalyzes its own palmitoylation. Palmitoylation is required for Golgi targeting.PTM Farnesylation at Cys-195 is required for Golgi targeting.PTM Geranylgeranylation at Cys-194 is mediated by the GGTase-3 complex and is required for Golgi SNARE complex assembly.SIMILARITY Belongs to the synaptobrevin family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
