  <bp:ProteinReference xmlns:bp="http://www.biopax.org/release/biopax-level3.owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" rdf:ID="ProteinReference44">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q96Q05 TRAPPC9</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TRAPPC9</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KIAA1882</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NIBP</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">T1</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref491" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Functions as an activator of NF-kappa-B through increased phosphorylation of the IKK complex. May function in neuronal cells differentiation. May play a role in vesicular transport from endoplasmic reticulum to Golgi.SUBUNIT Component of the multisubunit TRAPP (transport protein particle) complex, which includes at least TRAPPC2, TRAPPC2L, TRAPPC3, TRAPPC3L, TRAPPC4, TRAPPC5, TRAPPC8, TRAPPC9, TRAPPC10, TRAPPC11 and TRAPPC12. Directly interacts with IKBKB and MAP3K14.INTERACTION Processes and cell bodies of neurons.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS Expressed at high levels in muscle and kidney and to a lower extent in brain, heart and placenta.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the NIBP family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
