  <bp:ProteinReference xmlns:bp="http://www.biopax.org/release/biopax-level3.owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" rdf:ID="ProteinReference50">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q9UL33 TRAPPC2L</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TRAPPC2L</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HSPC126</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref509" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Plays a role in vesicular transport from endoplasmic reticulum to Golgi.SUBUNIT Component of the multisubunit TRAPP (transport protein particle) complex, which includes at least TRAPPC2, TRAPPC2L, TRAPPC3, TRAPPC3L, TRAPPC4, TRAPPC5, TRAPPC8, TRAPPC9, TRAPPC10, TRAPPC11 and TRAPPC12. Interacts with the heterodimer TRAPPC3-TRAPPC6A. Interacts with TRAPPC6A.INTERACTION Expressed in testis, liver, bladder, lung, spleen and brain, several cell lines and primary chondrocytes cell line.DISEASE The disease may be caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the TRAPP small subunits family. Sedlin subfamily.SEQUENCE CAUTION Intron retention.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
