  <bp:ProteinReference xmlns:bp="http://www.biopax.org/release/biopax-level3.owl#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" rdf:ID="ProteinReference65">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q5H9R7 PPP6R3</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PPP6R3</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C11orf23</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KIAA1558</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PP6R3</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SAPL</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SAPS3</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref761" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Regulatory subunit of protein phosphatase 6 (PP6). May function as a scaffolding PP6 subunit. May have an important role in maintaining immune self-tolerance.SUBUNIT Protein phosphatase 6 (PP6) holoenzyme is proposed to be a heterotrimeric complex formed by the catalytic subunit, a SAPS domain-containing subunit (PP6R) and an ankyrin repeat-domain containing regulatory subunit (ARS). Interacts with PPP6C and ANKRD28.INTERACTION Expressed in skeletal muscle, placenta, heart, pancreas, testis, brain, lung, liver, kidney, spleen, thymus, prostate, small intestine, colon and leukocytes.SIMILARITY Belongs to the SAPS family.SEQUENCE CAUTION Truncated N-terminus.SEQUENCE CAUTION Truncated N-terminus.SEQUENCE CAUTION Extended N-terminus.SEQUENCE CAUTION Truncated N-terminus.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
