    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TBC1D20 stimulates GTPase activity of RAB1, resulting in hydrolysis of GTP</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref802" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref803" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TBC1D20 was identified as a RAB1-specific GTPase activating protein (GAP) that stimulates RAB1-mediated GTP hydrolysis and plays roles in ER-to-Golgi trafficking. TBC1D20 is the only GAP that has been identified to block delivery of secretory cargo from the ER to the cell surface (Haas et al, 2007).</bp:comment>
